 Vexatious Litigant List |\n\nWage Garnishment\n\nForm number | Effective date | Form title\n---|---|---\nWG-001* | 1/1/2012 | Application For Earnings Withholding Order\nWG-002* | 1/1/2026 | Earnings Withholding Order\nWG-002 C | 1/1/2026 | Earnings Withholding Order (Chinese)\nWG-002 K | 1/1/2026 | Earnings Withholding Order (Korean)\nWG-002 S | 1/1/2026 | Earnings Withholding Order (Spanish)\nWG-002 V | 1/1/2026 | Earnings Withholding Order (Vietnamese)\nWG-003* | 1/1/2026 | Employee Instructions (Wage Garnishment)\nWG-003 C | 1/1/2026 | Employee Instructions (Wage Garnishment) (Chinese)\nWG-003 K | 1/1/2026 | Employee Instructions (Wage Garnishment) (Korean)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVexatious Litigant List | Judicial Branch of California (https://courts.ca.gov/news-reference/reports-publications/vexatious-litigant-list)\nciteturn1724search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; This optional form may be used by an individual that has been determined to be a vexatious litigant and who must obtain prior court approval to file any new litigation in which the vexatious litigant is not represented by an attorney. ... VL-125, Order on Application to Vacate Prefiling Order and Remove Plaintiff/Petitioner from Judicial Council Vexatious Litigant List ... If you have any questions about this list, please contact VexatiousLitigantGroup@jud.ca.gov.\nFiling new litigation means (1) commencing any civil action or proceeding, or (2) filing any petition, application, or motion (except a discovery motion) under the Family or Probate Code in the courts of California.\n\nVL-115, Order to File New Litigation by a Vexatious Litigant\nThis new optional form is the order portion of Request to File New Litigation by Vexatious Litigant (form VL-110).\n\nVL-120, Application for Order to Vacate Prefiling Order and Remove Plaintiff/Petitioner from Judicial Council Vexatious Litigant List\nThis new optional form may be used by a vexatious litigant to ask to be removed from the list of vexatious litigants who must obtain prefiling approval.\n\nVL-125, Order on Application to Vacate Prefiling Order and Remove Plaintiff/Petitioner from Judicial Council Vexatious Litigant List\nThis new optional form is an order to be used to grant or deny the vexatious litigant’s request to be removed from the list.\n\nContact\n\nIf you have any questions about this list, please contact VexatiousLitigantGroup@jud.ca.gov.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAPPENDIX A (https://courts.ca.gov/system/files?file=file%2Fappendix.pdf)\nciteturn1724search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.1 years ago; Crawled: 7 months ago; <tr><td>VL-110</td><td>9/1/2018</td><td>Request and Order to File New Litigation by Vexatious Litigant</td><td></td></tr> ... <tr><td>VL-125</td><td>9/1/2018</td><td>Order on Application to Vacate Prefiling Order and Remove Plaintiff/Petitioner From Judicial Council Vexatious Litigant List</td><td></td></tr>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms/all-by-category)\nciteturn1724search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago;   * CARE-125 Court Referral to the CARE Act Court Effective: July 1, 2026 ...   * UD-116 Declaration for Default Judgment by Court (Unlawful Detainer—Civ. ...   * VL-110 Request to File New Litigation by Vexatious Litigant Effective: September 1, 2018\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAPPENDIX A (https://courts.ca.gov/system/files?file=rules-court%2Fappendix.pdf)\nciteturn1724search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Crawled: 7 months ago; | UD-116 | 7/1/2003 | Declaration for Default Judgment by Court (Unlawful Detainer-Civ. ... | VL-125 | 9/1/2018 | Order on Application to Vacate Prefiling Order and Remove Plaintiff/Petitioner From Judicial Council Vexatious Lit